    43	#   Arms 65-72 assert that wiring exists and resolves; arm 16 asserts the
    44	#   settings.json route stays permanently unused. The two are complements:
    45	#   arm 16 is no longer a temporary marker, it is the boundary.
    46	#
    47	# ISOLATION
    48	#   Every behavioural arm pipes a synthetic PreToolUse payload into the hook
    49	#   under `env -u FATHOMDB_SEAT` (or an explicit FATHOMDB_SEAT=...). The hook is
    50	#   a pure stdin->stdout function: it never touches the filesystem, so the only
    51	#   temp state here is the mktemp -d fixture used by arm 16's positive control.
    52	#   Arms 65-72 are static parses of tracked files. No real file is ever written
