./dev/plans/runs/codex/DOC-HYGIENE-2/codex-T2b-20260725T205015Z.log:2392:      "summary": "STANDING RULING (HITL 2026-07-25): the ORCHESTRATOR is the PREFERRED commissioning mechanism; /goal is NOT. Order: (1) /orchestrate (alias /orch) HITL-opened session = default; (2) Steward-spawned background orchestrator Agent (subagent_type=orchestrator) when the Steward holds the loop — returns once, does NOT notify on stall, needs an anti-stall directive + git polling; (3) /goal complete 0.8.z ONLY on explicit HITL instruction for that run, never the Steward's own choice. Rationale: /orchestrate carries the repo's versioned guardrails (§0 preflight, worktree rules, codex §9, canary-then-max-3); /goal runs to a PROSE condition judged from the transcript, but a 0.8.x ladder is GATED not autonomous (X0/AC sign-off, publish, landings outside a mandate must STOP the loop) — precedent seq-81 had to scope /goal to 'Slice 0 X0 ONLY (hard stop after)', fighting the command's nature. Landed in 4 docs so every future steward AND orchestrator sees it: STEWARD-HANDOFF §9 (full rationale) + §1/§2/§8 call-sites, .claude/agents/steward.md (durable role contract, hard rule + loop line), .claude/commands/orchestrate.md, .claude/agents/orchestrator.md. NOT a deprecation of /goal — it remains a real built-in and the ~6 doc references to it are not wrong."
